{align:center|**DELINQUENT YOUTH**}

{align:justify|One day in 1995, at the guest house of Ngu Dai Son Monastery, there were twenty people waiting to ask for advice from Venerable Dieu Phap.These people came from the South and the North, taking turns asking questions.As for that wise Master, no matter how serious the problems raised by guests, He answered them very satisfactorily and easily.It's all like "As soon as you treat an illness, you see immediate results, shaking the person to wake up strongly", making everyone who listens feel like they are drinking nectar, the Dharma joy is full of fullness.}

{align:justify|– Venerable Master!I came from Taiwan to the mainland for medical examination.Three years ago I got seriously ill, then my whole body was in pain. The illness tortured me to the point where I couldn't eat or drink, couldn't sleep, my limbs were exhausted and I had no strength, the pain was extremely painful.Major hospitals in Taiwan did diagnoses but couldn't find the disease, they just said the child had "autonomic nervous system disorder"...I have had injections, needles, and medicine, but all have been ineffective.But taking too much medicine can have side effects.My body has been growing weaker and weaker; this time I came to Beijing for a checkup, and their diagnosis was identical to the one in Taiwan. No one has found the cause of the disease.I'm so depressed.Before returning to Taiwan, I wanted to go to Wutai Mountain to worship Bodhisattva. I just heard an old man traveling in the same car, constantly praising you. If you can cure me, then no matter how much it costs, I will pay it all...}

{align:justify|The person speaking is about thirty years old, has a thin body, and although his facial features are dignified, his expression is very gloomy.From him emanated a dark evil aura, compared to the good people sitting here, it was very contrasting.}

{align:justify|Master's voice was not high-pitched, but full of seriousness and coldness.He said:}
{align:justify|– You are not my disciple, no need to call me Master!Neither am I a physician, nor do I examine patients, much less dare to take your money. Please go home and seek other skilled healers!}

{align:justify|Having finished speaking, the Venerable ordered the guests to be dismissed, making those sitting there very surprised.He has never treated anyone like that before.This Taiwanese man (I forget his last name), felt embarrassed, his yellow-gray face suddenly turned red.}

{align:justify|He said angrily:}
{align:justify|– Doesn't Buddhism specialize in preaching compassion?Why can you examine someone else but not me?Do you still want to kick me out?While I have never offended you!}

{align:justify|Master's voice was sharp and serious:}
{align:justify|– Even if you dare to beat and scold your parents who gave birth to you and raised you – then why are you afraid of offending me?}

{align:justify|This statement made him instantly look like a deflated balloon.He was stunned, his eyes widened in surprise, his face turned from red to pale, unable to say a word.The guests in the guest house were silent, all eyes were on him.}

{align:justify|More than a minute passed, and he humbly said:}
{align:justify|– Sir…How can I know what you do, no one here knows you...}

{align:justify|– I don't need anyone else to tell me, because on your chest you have clearly written four words: "INFLATABLE DISRUPTION" very big!}

{align:justify|Hearing that, he was frightened and bent down to look at his chest to check. The eyes of everyone in the audience were glued to his chest, searching and examining, but did not see anything strange.}

{align:justify|At this time, he suddenly stood up, took a few steps forward, knelt down at the Venerable's feet, hit his head until it bled, and trembled and begged the Master to save him.}

{align:justify|He said he was a dishonest teenager since childhood.Things like stealing, fighting, cursing people...You have committed all of them.He didn't listen to what his parents taught him, then was expelled from school, he wandered around and joined a gangster gang.He specializes in collecting protection money, defrauding girls, robbing...There is no evil that cannot be done.His father was angry and hit him, but he hit him back, causing his father to fall to the ground.He even pushed his mother down and declared that if anyone wanted to discipline him, they would set fire to the whole house.His father was old and so angry that he became bedridden, and his mother had to take care of him every day.And I'm afraid that he's out there creating trouble and sowing evil, and his parents will soon pass away one after another...}

{align:justify|He knelt towards Venerable Dieu Phap to declare his past cruel acts. When he mentioned his parents' passing away, he couldn't help but choke up and burst into tears.So a stubborn, stubborn "rock" that was difficult to tame was softened by the Master's mighty virtue, and had to bow its head in prostration...}

{align:justify|In my heart, I was extremely impressed. It seemed like good and bad people were written on their bodies in Master's eyes. He could see through them all!}

{align:justify|– Okay, get up!The monk gently said - If you call me Master, you must listen to my teachings, can you do that?}

{align:justify|He happily said:}
{align:justify|– Yes!Yes!I can do it.I will definitely correct my mistakes and repent, vowing to be a good person from now on.}

{align:justify|– Okay, I accept you as a disciple.}

{align:justify|He happily nodded his head.People in the auditorium also stood up and respectfully clasped their hands.Today they witnessed a touching scene, so they were filled with joy and praise.}

{align:justify|The monk told a young monk}
{align:justify|- Take him to the main hall, teach him how to worship and repent, let him bow a thousand times in the main hall, and when he has finished apologizing, come back out.}

{align:justify|After an hour and a half, when that Taiwanese man returned to pay his respects to Master, he looked bright, lively, and completely different from before.He recounted that he had made a solemn vow before the Buddha, taking refuge in the Triple Gem from now on, mending his ways, and turning toward virtue. And after making the following vow, he felt comfortable all over, as if his illness had healed.}

{align:justify|Everything that happened before our eyes made people at the scene endlessly praise.}

{align:justify|Buddha said: "All sentient beings have Buddha nature and can become Buddhas.Just because of false thoughts and attachments, one cannot attain enlightenment."Buddha said again: “The sea of ​​suffering is boundless, turn around and see the shore.Let go of the butcher's knife and immediately become a Buddha"...Before everyone's eyes, this former errant youth who had committed rebellious unfilial deeds and suffered retribution through relentless illness, was now transformed. Luckily, I met the enlightened Master and realized how to repent and change my mind.This is exactly the experience and evidence that the sutras once said: "Buddha is the true great physician, the Buddha Dharma can cure forty-eight thousand diseases"...}

{align:justify|I once again witnessed the immense power of Buddha Dharma.“The Buddha Dharma is within the world; enlightenment is not separate from worldly life.” As long as we live conscientiously without the slightest heedlessness, our daily conduct will always accord with the Dharma, dispelling any misconception that Buddhism is mere superstition.}

{align:justify|COMMENTS:}
{align:justify|The story of ILLEGAL TEENAGER is eloquent proof of the saying "Disobedience and filial piety" is the cause, constant illness and suffering are the retribution.A young Taiwanese man once beat his parents, declared the house on fire, causing his parents to die in pain - that is the most serious crime of filial piety among the five precepts.When he met Venerable Dieu Phap, he didn't need anyone to tell him anything but clearly "saw" the four words on his chest.This reminds us that karma is never lost, and that in the eyes of wise masters, the human mind is like an open book.Fortunately, when he sincerely repented, hit his head and bled, and bowed thousands of times, his karma was immediately transformed and his illness disappeared.The story affirms: "The sea of ​​suffering is boundless, turning around is the shore."No matter how serious the crime is, with just one thought of sincere repentance, taking refuge in the Three Jewels and practicing, one can turn evil into good, from hell on earth to the light.}

{align:center|**UNEXPECTED RESPONSE**}

Five years ago, Mr. Ha was over 40 years old, his son Cun was already 12. From a young age Cun was stubborn, willful. After school he not only played but refused to study, liked to fight and often skipped school. Parents and teachers were at a loss. Cun s behavior caused unrest in the whole family.

Embracing the Buddhist path, Ms. Ha s younger sister having faith in the Buddha, wanted to use Buddhist teachings to educate the boy, to help her brother. She brought him to consult the Venerable...
